Browser Context in Playwright is an isolated browser session similar to an incognito window. 
Multiple contexts can run inside a single browser instance while maintaining separate cookies, 
cache, and authentication states. It helps in fast parallel execution, multi-user testing, and efficient resource management

Simple Real-Time Example

Suppose you want to test:

User A shopping cart
User B shopping cart

at the same time.

Instead of opening 2 separate browsers, Playwright creates:

One Browser
   ├── Context 1 → User A
   └── Context 2 → User B

Both users remain isolated.
Why Browser Context is Important
Benefits
1. Session Isolation

Each context has separate:

login session
cookies
cache

No data sharing.

2. Faster Execution

Creating contexts is lightweight compared to launching full browsers.

3. Parallel Testing

Multiple users/scenarios can run simultaneously.

4. Multi-User Testing

Useful for:

Admin/User flow
Chat applications
Ecommerce checkout
Role-based testing
Architecture Understanding
Browser
   ↓
Browser Context
   ↓
Page/Tabs

One context can have multiple pages/tabs.
